          "text": "For example, a critical type of customer information may be Customer Perception; a characterization of their viewpoint in relation to a specific topic. Another critical type of information for your business may be Product Offering, which has a relationship to Customer Perception where your business needs to know that perception of that product to inform internal planning. A Sales Lead (stakeholder) has the ability to assess customer needs (Customer Analysis – a business capability), which includes the subjective ability (not in a form reducible to a data field), through experience, to assess Customer Perception. The Sales Lead, armed with stored data such as previous sales volume in a customer relationship management system and product characteristics in a product data management system, makes a final recommendation on product development based on their subjective view of Customer Perception. A sample of this relationship is shown in Figure 5-1.",
